      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Shasta%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city incorporated on May 31, 1905, and officially adopted the name 'City of Mount Shasta' after a 1922 vote.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Shasta%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mount Shasta receives more precipitation than the nearby semiarid north because the volcano forces moist air upward, creating a rain shadow effect.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Shasta%2C_California",
